---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — The Oracles"
  description="One studio, one law. We tell the truth as a story across every aspect of life: church, state, family, market, and the individual."
  path="/about"
>
  <section class="vhero">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 class="vhero__title">One&nbsp;law,<br />one <span class="accent">aim.</span></h1>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="measure" style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:3.5rem;">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow vermillion">What is The Oracles?</p>
        <p class="lead">
          We&rsquo;re a studio that does our best to orient ourselves around the
          beauty of God&rsquo;s law and the weight of a good story.
        </p>
        <p class="lead">
          Our name has its roots in the Hebrew word <span dir="rtl" style="font-family:var(--font-display); font-size:1.4em;">מַשָּׂא</span>
          <span class="muted">(pronounced <em>mas-saw</em>)</span>, used about a
          dozen times in Isaiah to introduce a word from God: a burden, a
          pronouncement, an oracle.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow vermillion">One law, all of life</p>
        <p class="lead">
          God&rsquo;s law orders every aspect of life, and each element has its
          own expression.
        </p>
        <p class="lead">
          Every part of our life has a story connected to the way God made
          things to work, His law.
        </p>
        <p class="lead" style="margin-top:0.5rem;">
          <strong>Church</strong>: Redemption &amp; Revelation. &nbsp;
          <strong>State</strong>: We the People. &nbsp;
          <strong>Market</strong>: A Collective Garden. &nbsp;
          <strong>Family</strong>: Foundation of Society. &nbsp;
          <strong>Individual</strong>: Self Government.
        </p>
        <p class="lead" style="margin-top:1rem;">
          A ministry film, a campaign, a wedding, a construction site, a personal
          struggle. They look unrelated, but they share a core truth: they
          flourish when operating consistently with the way things are.
          That&rsquo;s the story we want to tell.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow vermillion">How we got here</p>
        <p class="lead">Two friends, more than a decade in.</p>
        <p class="lead">
          One had been trying to share the beauty of God&rsquo;s world and kept
          struggling to find the form. The other had been living in that beauty
          and hadn&rsquo;t seen it as clearly as he&rsquo;d thought. We needed each
          other to see it, and we needed each other to share it.
        </p>
        <p class="lead">
          What looked like two halves of a split thing, God knit back together in
          The Oracles.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section rule-top">
    <p class="eyebrow vermillion">Who we are</p>
    <p class="lead measure">
      Aaron is technical, obsessed with the details. Dabraham barely notices the
      details, but knows exactly how they&rsquo;ll make you feel. We need each
      other to make anything at all.
    </p>
    <div class="two-up measure-wide">
      <figure style="margin:0;">
        <div class="person__photo"><img src="/images/dabe.jpg" alt="Dabraham Searcy" loading="lazy" /></div>
        <figcaption>
          <p class="person__name">Dabraham</p>
          <p class="lead">A seasoned illustrator who directs, the creative influence and primary storyteller.</p>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure style="margin:0;">
        <div class="person__photo"><img src="/images/aaron.jpg" alt="Aaron Sanford" loading="lazy" /></div>
        <figcaption>
          <p class="person__name">Aaron</p>
          <p class="lead">A former pastor who shoots and cuts, the DP/editor who brings the vision to life.</p>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block-ink">
    <p class="eyebrow">Psalm 1 &middot; the measure</p>
    <blockquote class="h1" style="color:var(--color-paper); max-width:64rem;">
      His delight is in the law of the Lord,<br />
      <span style="display:inline-block; padding-left:1em;">and on his law he meditates day and night.</span>
    </blockquote>
    <a href="/contact" class="link-slash link-slash--paper">/ Got a project? Contact the studio</a>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
